Subject: Cantor Resident Service

Description: A bounded, authenticated, explicitly configured local resident service that shares one verified immutable Cantor generation across callers and atomically activates operator-published replacements without acquiring independent semantic authority.

@ [source] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-29_cantor_resident_service_activation\Dictated_Cantor_Resident_Service_Activation_Source.sop
@ [manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-07-29_cantor_resident_service_activation\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Resident_Service.exploded.sop
@ [execution_surface] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Execution_Surface_Profile.sop
@ [prepared_runtime] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Prepared_Runtime.sop
@ [self_hosting] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Self_Hosting_Ingestion.sop

& [ResidentServiceIdentity] is the activated bounded service
  + [specification_uuid] is 276ad3fd-d1fa-4b32-9bdd-5cd572bf1ece
  + [service_profile] is cantor-resident-service/0.1
  + [server_executable] is cantord
  + [client_executable] is cantorctl
  + [semantic_authority] is only cantor_core over admitted signed packages
  + [service_authority] is local runtime lifecycle under operator-pinned artifacts
  + [implementation_status] is authorized
  = must: preserve exact ProtocolRequest and ProtocolResponse semantics
  - never: compile packages, mutate trust, interpret SOP independently, or perform exterior effects

& [ServiceConfiguration] is strict operator startup authority
  + [schema] is cantor-service-config/0.1
  + [listen_address] is explicit loopback IP and port
  + [activation_path] is the only descriptor refresh may read
  + [allowed_environment_root] contains every candidate environment
  + [auth_token_path] contains exactly 64 hexadecimal characters representing 256 bits
  + [max_frame_bytes] is from 1024 through 1048576 so one bounded fault envelope is always representable
  + [max_connections] is positive and no greater than 256
  + [read_timeout_ms] is from 1 through 60000
  + [write_timeout_ms] is from 1 through 60000
  = must: deny unknown fields, relative authority paths, non-loopback addresses, duplicate paths, invalid limits, and non-regular files
  = must: start no listener until every authority artifact and runtime generation passes

& [ActivationDescriptor] is immutable operator publication
  + [schema] is cantor-environment-activation/0.1
  + [sequence] is positive and monotonically increasing for refresh
  + [environment_path] is absolute, canonical, and root-contained
  + [environment_file_sha256] is SHA-256 of exact environment bytes
  + [descriptor_digest] is SHA-256 of canonical descriptor serialization
  + [generation_id] is derived independently by PreparedRuntime
  = must: verify file size, exact digest, strict JSON, environment version, signatures, trust, package set, fabric structure, and PreparedRuntime construction
  = may: activate a prior environment as rollback only through a new higher sequence
  - never: accept a request-selected path or modify operator artifacts

& [ServiceEnvelope] is cantor-service-protocol/0.1
  + [request] is protocol_version, request_id, auth_token, and one tagged operation
  + [response] is protocol_version, request_id, disposition, active binding, optional typed result, and fault set
  + [active_binding] is generation_id, activation_sequence, activation_digest, and environment_file_sha256
  + [operations] is status, execute, refresh, and shutdown
  + [framing] is one bounded JSON object followed by LF per connection
  = must: reject unknown fields and unsupported versions
  = must: return one bounded JSON response followed by LF and close
  = must: compare fixed-length token bytes without early exit
  - never: echo, hash into public diagnostics, or otherwise disclose the authentication token

& [StatusOperation] is bounded operational inspection
  + [result] is service profile, active binding, RuntimeGeneration, PreparedRuntimeMetrics, active package identifiers, uptime milliseconds, accepted connections, rejected connections, worker panic count, completed requests, and refresh count
  = must: exclude secrets, source contents, environment contents, and caller histories

& [ExecuteOperation] is exact core delegation
  + [input] is one unchanged cantor-protocol/0.1 ProtocolRequest
  + [snapshot] is one complete acquired ActiveServiceGeneration
  + [output] is the exact PreparedRuntime ProtocolResponse
  = must: release the active generation lock before semantic execution
  = must: bind the service response to the generation that executed the request
  - never: repair, broaden, default, or reinterpret caller scope and package expectations

& [RefreshOperation] is compare-and-activate
  + [input] is expected_generation_id and expected_activation_sequence
  + [candidate_source] is only the pinned activation_path
  + [preparation] is complete strict load and preflight outside the active-state write lock
  + [activation] is one exact comparison and whole-generation swap
  + [success] is candidate sequence greater than current with a distinct complete valid generation
  + [failure] leaves the prior generation active
  = must: reject stale expectation, non-increasing sequence, unchanged generation, tamper, invalid trust, invalid package, and concurrent replacement loss
  - never: invalidate a valid active generation merely because candidate preparation fails

& [ShutdownOperation] is explicit local lifecycle control
  + [input] is expected_generation_id
  + [success] stops new acceptance after returning its response
  + [acquired_work] may finish against its exact immutable snapshot
  = must: reject stale generation and invalid authentication
  - never: expose unauthenticated remote shutdown

& [TransportBoundary] is explicit bounded loopback TCP
  + [listener_default] is absent
  + [activation] is running cantord with exactly one configuration path
  + [address] is IPv4 or IPv6 loopback only
  + [connection_model] is bounded concurrent workers and one request per connection
  + [timeouts] are enforced for reads and writes
  + [frame_limit] is enforced before JSON decoding
  + [diagnostics] are bounded and secret-free
  = must: reject non-loopback bind even when configured
  = must: reject connection excess visibly when a response can be written safely
  - never: claim encryption, remote authentication, multi-user authorization, or denial-of-service resistance beyond the declared local bounds

& [RestartAndRecovery] is artifact-derived
  + [startup_generation] is reconstructed from unchanged configuration, token metadata, activation, and environment
  + [same_artifacts] produce the same RuntimeGeneration and activation digest
  + [failed_startup] listens nowhere and exits nonzero
  + [failed_refresh] preserves the prior active generation
  + [rollback] is a higher-sequence operator activation of a previously valid environment
  + [direct_fallback] is cantor embedded CLI and standalone cantor-mcp
  = must: document publication ordering as environment first then activation descriptor

& [ThinClient] is cantorctl
  + [configuration] is the same strict service configuration
  + [token] is read from auth_token_path and excluded from arguments and output
  + [commands] is status, query, inspect, refresh, and shutdown
  + [structured_input] is file or standard input
  + [structured_output] is exactly one ServiceResponse on standard output
  = must: enforce local frame bounds and timeouts
  = must: verify request identity and service protocol identity in the response

& [RequirementSet] is traceable
  + [RS-001] is strict configuration, activation, request, response, and fault schemas
  + [RS-002] is startup fail-closed trust, path, digest, and fabric validation
  + [RS-003] is exact embedded, prepared, service-library, and live-transport semantic equivalence
  + [RS-004] is authenticated loopback-only operation and complete token non-disclosure
  + [RS-005] is bounded frames, connections, timeouts, messages, and outputs
  + [RS-006] is atomic monotonic refresh with stale, replay, tamper, and invalid-candidate rejection
  + [RS-007] is deterministic restart, rollback shape, and exact-generation shutdown
  + [RS-008] is concurrent readers observe complete old or complete new generations only
  + [RS-009] is a reproducible operator workflow and direct fallback
  + [RS-010] is measured round-trip, refresh, and restart behavior with correctness accounting

& [ImplementationProgression] is bounded
  + [phase_1] is shared core environment preflight
  + [phase_2] is strict service models and artifact loading
  + [phase_3] is immutable active generation and refresh
  + [phase_4] is loopback server and thin client
  + [phase_5] is equivalence, fault, restart, concurrency, security, and measurement proof
  + [later] is sessions, notifications, faculties, provider pools, write authority, and distributed junctions only through separate SJS activation

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the seven-fold canonicalization
  + [fold_1_subject] is continue product work by activating the next dependency-ready Cantor runtime slice
  + [fold_2_boundary] is shared local read-only residency inside and independent semantics, remote exposure, effects, and autonomous activation outside
  + [fold_3_data] is configuration, token capability, activation descriptor, environment bytes, runtime generation, request, response, status, transition, metrics, and fault
  + [fold_4_governance] is source preservation, explicit listener activation, root containment, token secrecy, signed environment preflight, monotonic compare-and-swap, and direct rollback
  + [fold_5_solution] is strict loader, immutable generation, loopback service, thin client, tests, measurements, proof, and operator documentation
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is path escape, token leak, remote bind, oversized input, stale refresh, candidate invalidation, mixed generation, adapter drift, and silent fallback
  + [fold_7_lock] is one bounded resident read-only service while broader runtime claims remain inactive

& [CantorResidentServiceSatisfactionSignature] is the valid implementation authority
  + [signature_protocol_uuid] is ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
